  "id": "COMPOUND:30035 - PROTEIN:5836",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Erysimoside may have a relationship with HUVEC through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Erysimoside to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, a compound that ultimately targets HUVEC. The second pathway connects Erysimoside to Ataxin-2, which is targeted by Diplotrin A, which also targets HUVEC. The third pathway shows Erysimoside targeting Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by 5-O-Methylcelebixanthone, which in turn targets HUVEC. These findings collectively indicate that Erysimoside may exert its effects on HUVEC via different molecular mechanisms, possibly through the modulation of enzymes involved in lipid metabolism or other cellular processes. The evidence suggests a potential role for Erysimoside in influencing HUVEC function, though the exact mechanisms and the strength of the relationship remain to be fully elucidated.",
